  "title": "The 3rd on the bottom",
  "summary": "Move the root up an octave and the 3rd becomes the lowest note.",
  "minutes": 5,
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "First inversion",
      "body": "Take C E G and move the C up an octave: E G C. Now the 3rd is lowest. That is **first inversion**.\n\n**Why it matters:** First inversion sounds lighter than root position, and it lets the bass climb or fall step by step. On a chart, C/E is C in first inversion.",
